Metal: optional sync-path tracer (ACPP_METAL_TRACE_SYNC=1)

Diagnostic only, inert unless ACPP_METAL_TRACE_SYNC=1.

The Metal backend contains one structural way to produce a command buffer that
stays "scheduled" forever with error == nil: a GPU wait whose value is signalled
only from a CPU listener block. Two such sites exist, in the host-to-host
memcpy path and the staged host-to-device path, and both are reachable only
when _pending_cpu_event is non-zero. The host-to-host branch is the sole writer
of that field, so it alone bootstraps the cycle.

These counters report whether the cycle is reachable in a given workload:

  h2h_total      host-to-host memcpy seen
  h2h_listener   ... took the listener branch (bootstrap)
  gpu_wait_armed a command buffer encoded a wait on a CPU-signalled value
  h2d_listener   staged host-to-device took the listener branch

First occurrence of each is reported immediately; totals are printed at exit.

Measured on WarpX 2D Langmuir (128^2, ppc=4, 500 steps, M4 Pro, macOS 26):
all four counters are 0, i.e. the cycle is not reachable in that configuration
and cannot explain a completion-loss hang there.

